Fuzzing hivex using the American Fuzzy Lop (AFL++) fuzzer
=========================================================

The fuzzing/ subdirectory contains support for fast, persistent
mode fuzzing using AFL++.

You will need to recompile hivex with AFL + Clang instrumentation:

  export AFL_USE_ASAN=1
  ./configure \
      --enable-fuzzing \
      --disable-shared \
      CC=/usr/bin/afl-clang-fast \
      CXX=/usr/bin/afl-clang-fast++ \
      --disable-ocaml \
      --disable-perl \
      --disable-python \
      --disable-ruby
  make clean
  make

This should generate a binary 'fuzzing/fuzz-hivex' which uses AFL++
"persistent mode", see:
https://github.com/AFLplusplus/AFLplusplus/blob/stable/instrumentation/README.persistent_mode.md

images/minimal and images/special may be used as initial test cases:

  mkdir -p testcase_dir sync_dir
  cp images/minimal images/special testcase_dir/

Run multiple copies of afl-fuzz.  Usually you should run 1 master (-M)
and as many slaves (-S) as you can:

Master:

  mkdir -p sync_dir
  afl-fuzz -i testcase_dir -o sync_dir -m 0 -M fuzz01 fuzzing/fuzz-hivex

Slaves:

  # replace fuzzNN with fuzz02, fuzz03, etc.
  afl-fuzz -i testcase_dir -o sync_dir -m 0 -S fuzzNN fuzzing/fuzz-hivex
